  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nNative-Anthropic routes emitted thinking budgets from an invented flat map (`512..8192` by effort name) whenever any effort was set — regardless of what the model accepts. Modern Claude models expose a native effort channel instead; sending them a synthetic budget is a guaranteed-400 risk, and Part IV §1 bans invented limits besides.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe encoder now consults the same `ModelReasoningCapability` lookup the gating layer uses: models reporting **effort** control get the native effort channel; models reporting **budget** control keep enabled+budget_tokens clamped to their real limit with the documented 1024 floor; **unknown models stay byte-identical** to today (§163 identity property, asserted by test). The invented map is retired exactly where a confirmed channel exists.\n\nScope note: landed at both body-building call sites so the fix is live in production, not just in the request builder.\n\n## Verification\n\n41 new tests across a capability matrix (known-effort / known-budget / unknown × explicit budget / effort-only / sub-floor), byte-identity assertions for unknowns, zero regressions in the pre-existing 286-test baseline including the byte-baseline guard. §66 mutations ×4 caught by name (effort branch dropped, floor clamp removed, absence guard disabled, membership return nulled); ruff/format/ty clean. MINOR slot **5.53.0**.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nAn effort-only intent arriving UNGATED at the encoder on a budget-only model still takes the legacy map — unreachable in production (every policy passes gating first), documented in the lane deviations.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
