     "date": "2026-08-24T19:03:04Z"
    },
    "message": "feat(providers): capability-aware Anthropic reasoning budgets\n\nThe native Messages encoder emitted {type: enabled, budget_tokens: N} out\nof FCC's invented effort-to-budget map whenever any effort was set,\nregardless of what the upstream model accepts -- a guaranteed 400 on\nmodels that speak the native effort channel instead.\n\nbuild_anthropic_messages_body now takes the resolved\nModelReasoningCapability alongside the gated policy:\n\n- effort-known models get output_config.effort passthrough (the\n  documented GA shape) plus the existing adaptive-thinking default;\n- budget-known models keep enabled+budget_tokens, raised to the\n  documented 1024 floor;\n- unknown capability reproduces the historical body byte for byte, so\n  the invented map is retired only on routes where metadata confirms a\n  channel.\n\nThe channel decision lives in application/reasoning_gating.py as the\nshared native_wire_effort helper; AnthropicMessagesProvider resolves the\ncapability per request through the same models.dev lookup the router\nuses. All new guards are mutation-checked; unknown-model bodies are\npinned by a byte-identity matrix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
